    <paragraph>For the following exercises, use the limit definition of derivative to show that the derivative does not exist at $$x = a$$ for each of the given functions.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="41" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = x^{1/3},x = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$lim x \to 0 - x 1 / 3 - 0 x - 0 = lim x \to 0 - 1 x 2 / 3 = \infty lim x \to 0 - x 1 / 3 - 0 x - 0 = lim x \to 0 - 1 x 2 / 3 = \infty$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
